  "finding": "No cutoff reaches the target while the compatibility test is still testing anything. Joint acceptance equals the square of the per-fold rate throughout, so the folds are independent and cross-fitting squares the miss probability: joint 0.95 needs per-fold 0.975. The cutoffs that deliver it accept 9.8 of 10 thresholds on average, and by critical=6 the whole grid every time. Retuning the constant cannot fix this; the hard stable-prefix rule is what wants redesigning."
